+## Live verification after both repairs
+
+Runtime settings now reserve autonomy for `neko` from startup. Both components
+were reloaded through the trial lifecycle; unattended recovery is enabled.
+The local Qwen service and existing Neko main session stayed available.
+
+The first 55 seconds after reconnect still contained one query-budget cap and
+no body action. Therefore this does not claim that prompts eliminate every
+query-only turn or the model's planning latency. At 10:34:28 Neko naturally
+dispatched task `525f09c8b6dd43ef8942e7bafd2c994c`, without any diagnostic task
+or chat injection. Native execution logged `!digDown(10)` and ten successful
+stone breaks. The next 55-second passive capture attributed 16 blocks of
+vertical movement, inventory changes, and 17 active snapshots to that actual
+mission. It had zero kernel commits, handoff failures, or tool-budget caps.
+Artifact: `query-loop-actual-task-20261009.json`.
+
+The verifier now correlates mission IDs, executed body code, active telemetry,
+and world changes. The earlier claim-plus-movement verdict was corrected to
+false in `query-loop-after-20261009.json`. This confirms recovery of real
+autonomous action execution, not completion of the whole mining goal or
+long-term unattended survival. Health checks confirmed the local model loaded,
+YUI active/ready, plugin connected, LAN viewer online, and guardian running:
+`neko-stuck-final-health-20261009.json`.
